# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0017925> (T-cell immunodeficiency with epidermodysplasia verruciformis)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Orphanet:324294") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0017925> "T-cell immunodeficiency with epidermodysplasia verruciformis is a rare primary immunodeficiency characterized by increased susceptibility to infection by human papillomavirus, presenting in childhood with disseminated flat wart-like cutaneous lesions. Burkitt lymphoma has also been reported. Whilst total T-cell counts are normal, there is impaired TCR signaling, profound peripheral naive T-cell lymphopenia with memory T-cells displaying an exhaustion phenotype.")
